{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/p2ppsr/interop/pulls/26","id":5286381195,"node_id":"PR_kwDOUePwzM8AAAABOxfGiw","html_url":"https://github.com/p2ppsr/interop/pull/26","diff_url":"https://github.com/p2ppsr/interop/pull/26.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/p2ppsr/interop/pull/26.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/p2ppsr/interop/issues/26","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/p2ppsr/interop/pulls/26/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/p2ppsr/interop/pulls/26/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/p2ppsr/interop/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/p2ppsr/interop/issues/26/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/p2ppsr/interop/statuses/58e0c45b6cdac06cbf351292249c5a059168fced","number":26,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Integrate Go native wallet conformance fixes and evidence","user":{"login":"ty-everett","id":23272461,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMjcyNDYx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23272461?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ty-everett","html_url":"https://github.com/ty-everett","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ty-everett/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ty-everett/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ty-everett/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ty-everett/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ty-everett/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ty-everett/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ty-everett/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ty-everett/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ty-everett/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Native wallet calls exposed validation, allowance accounting, permission scope, transaction proof and observer-ordering gaps in the Go-backed ITCVE-1 profile. This PR integrates the exact wallet candidate from [Yours PR368](https://github.com/yours-org/yours-wallet/pull/368), repairs the Go storage and native evidence paths, and retains all original failed attempts. It follows merged PR24.\n\nThe optional ITCVE-1 4.7 / ISI-4 5.7 profile freezes 416 inputs and the exact e360e67 extension. It retains all 698 predicate identities, nine native browser contexts and the complete provider/funding/shutdown joins. Historical profiles, artifacts and oracles remain immutable.\n\nThe changes cover:\n\n- Go Wallet Storage compatibility for public contracts, action references, proof ancestry, transaction batching, dust/merge accounting, SQLite retries and caller-known inputs, connected to Go Overlay Services and ChainTracks through the existing component selectors.\n- Public CWI validation and structured errors, signed transaction/result checks, stored certificate keyring revealers, request-keyed native prompts, peer-scoped linkage grants, discovery's default consent flag, and per-origin allowance progress without dropping other pending debits. The retained wallet CI passes 269 tests / 1,839 expectations and all four bundles.\n- Permission sequences, basket and pagination boundaries, certificate rejection, transaction branches and independently bound trace predicates. The pinned contract's literal `identityKey:false` rejection has its own new major extension oracle; ordinary child derivation and true identity retrieval remain positive controls.\n- Strict prior-fixture replay on positive imports: at most one exact previously accepted raw transaction, independently verified signed AtomicBEEF/mined proof, and an exact earlier creation window. Rejected calls still require zero receipts and unchanged complete owned state. Every receipt and ancestor remains in the final parent checks. Capture and independent children select the same published program and oracle from the parent profile.\n- Append-only owned producer receipts with complete provider-local provenance through shutdown, all 31 controlled destinations, stable pre-click screen capture, exact trusted-click binding and durable active-provider observations. Denied-spend and full ancestor checks remain mandatory.\n- Two final native image layers with complete inherited/overlaid byte, mode, owner, symlink and runtime-configuration checks. Bounded split ZIP publication preserves large original artifact bytes. Source9 separately replays the unchanged original native archive and Rust criteria with zero new native sessions.\n\nThis draft contains the complete implementation and frozen criteria. Final native qualification is pending the draft PR's full-branch Foundation check; it will then execute two clean698-predicate repetitions and both48-predicate Rust joins before this PR is marked ready.\n\nCompleted validation: pinned Node24 local synthesis1,744PASS/91SKIP, core230PASS, five Python tests, typecheck/catalog/standards, and actual two-provider Go fixture-replay controls. [Wallet CI](https://github.com/yours-org/yours-wallet/actions/runs/43306868169) passes269tests/1,839expectations and all four bundles. [Source9 reevaluation](https://github.com/p2ppsr/interop/actions/runs/43318146899) and its independent frozen replay preserve all220artifact members and unchanged original186-member native archive/280 native/77 integration/48 Rust criteria per repetition.\n\nThe branch's journal-history check passes against accepted `main`. The earlier index-replacement history failure remains documented with both index versions retained; the history gate is unchanged. Native13 has not been dispatched yet.\n\nThe final native execution source is recorded independently of the later evidence-publication commit. The journal-only correction preserves the original canceled-attempt manifest bytes and changes no frozen native/runtime/evaluator criterion. The retained source9 reevaluation and its independent frozen replay preserve the original 186-member native archive, 280 original predicates, 77 integration predicates and 48 Rust predicates per repetition.\n\nThe signed-satoshi `listActions` normative conflict and the enumerated capability, interpretation, calendar and representation requirements remain explicit. Added predicates and verified engineering evidence do not establish complete BRC100 conformance or certification. The [results report](https://github.com/p2ppsr/interop/blob/58e0c45b6cdac06cbf351292249c5a059168fced/docs/native-conformance-results-2026-11-12.md) links every exact scope, failed sample, artifact and replay.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-12T22:37:18Z","updated_at":"2026-11-12T22:37:18Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"d7b1a726aa406f05f9a99b758a61e4f40a10f42e","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"p2ppsr:codex/native-wallet-closure-20261111","ref":"codex/native-wallet-closure-20261111","repo":{"id":1373892812,"node_id":"R_kgDOUePwzA","name":"interop","full_name":"p2ppsr/interop","owner":{"login":"p2ppsr","id":65189042,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjY1MTg5MDQy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65189042?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/p2ppsr","html_url":"https://github.com/p2ppsr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p2ppsr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p2ppsr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p2ppsr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p2ppsr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p2ppsr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p2ppsr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p2ppsr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p2ppsr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p2ppsr/received_events","type":